{"slug":"barney-frank","qid":"Q537287","name":"Barney Frank","desc":"American politician (1940–2026)","article":"Barney Frank","born":"1940-03-31","died":"2026-05-19","birthplace":"Bayonne","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MA-04","f":1981,"u":2013},{"t":"Massachusetts House of Representatives","w":"","f":1973,"u":1981}],"summary":"Barney Frank (March 31, 1940 – May 19, 2026) was an American politician who served as a member of the U.S. House of Representatives from Massachusetts from 1981 to 2013. A Democrat, Frank served as chairman of the House Financial Services Committee from 2007 to 2011 and was a leading co-sponsor of the 2010 Dodd–Frank Act, the primary legislative response to the 2007–2008 financial crisis. Frank, a resident of Newton, Massachusetts, was considered the most prominent gay politician in the United States during his time in Congress.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":126194,"s":53.9,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":203032,"s":67.95,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":176513,"s":98.48,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":2004,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":219260,"s":77.74,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":2002,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":166125,"s":98.99,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":200638,"s":74.9,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1998,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":148340,"s":98.42,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1996,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":183844,"s":71.64,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":168942,"s":99.5,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":182633,"s":67.69,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":143473,"s":62.41,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"MA-04","p":"D","v":169729,"s":70.31,"w":true,"n":"Barney Frank"},{"y":1986,"o"